      "writtenOn": "2023-07-18T08:12:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a good point. I\u0027m also considering testing the memory management to `vmbase_example`, but that still won\u0027t allow us to reach this function easily. As `shared_alloc` is only called in the `vmbase::HalImpl`, and `vmbase_example` plugs in its own `HalImpl` so we still don\u0027t access this function.\n\nOtherwise, we will have a regression test (fails without this adjustment) when testing the rialto vsock connection [1]. Because when we connect the virtio vsock device, we always add a header of 44 bytes to its rx virtqueue, thus allocating a buffer of 44 bytes here.\n\n[1] https://r.android.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/2658870/1/rialto/tests/test.rs",
      "parentUuid": "8a3a6df1_59338896",
      "revId": "faa515a644d40bd2b3b066818458518517d916a0",
