      "side": 1,
      "message": "This might not cover the whole story as, looking at the code of [`FrameAllocator::alloc_aligned`](https://docs.rs/buddy_system_allocator/latest/src/buddy_system_allocator/frame.rs.html#93):\n```\nlet size \u003d max(layout.size().next_power_of_two(), layout.align());\n```\nso you\u0027ll still hit the bug if `layout.align() \u003e layout.size.next_power_of_two()` (which might be a theoretical case for now but we want our software to be robust). Instead, could we (re)define `layout` with that `size`?",
